CommitDate: Fri Sep 18 07:41:14 2026 -0500

    fix(api): preserve YAML sequence item continuations
    
    parseYAMLSequence built the synthetic mapping for an inline sequence item
    ("- name: q") at the SEQUENCE's baseIndent, while that item's continuation
    lines sit deeper. parseYAMLMapping only consumes lines at its baseIndent, so
    every continuation key was dropped — silently, because the collection loop had
    already advanced past those lines. The damage showed on the real spec: OpenAPI
    parameter metadata (in/required/schema/description) never reached
    /openapi.json, and only 5 of the 7 source enum arrays arrived.
    
    Resolve the synthetic block's indent from the inline mapping's own column (just
    past the "- " marker), lowered to the shallowest collected line so a deeper
    non-key line — block-scalar content under `description: |` — cannot drag the
    mapping past its own scalar, then parse the block at that indent.
    
    Verified live: the served /openapi.json now carries all 15 parameters with
    in + schema, servers/tags descriptions, and all 7 source enums as non-empty
    arrays. Regression coverage asserts key SETS and the nested flow-sequence enums
    and fails on the pre-fix parser.
    
    Addresses OB-GAP-072
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
